OUTLINE

I. Introduction

* Brief introduction to HTML content sections
* Introduce the three elements:

  * `<article>`
  * `<section>`
  * `<aside>`
* Explain that these elements help organize webpage content

II. `<article>` Element

* Definition of `<article>`
* Purpose: used for standalone or independent content
* Examples:

  * News articles
  * Blog posts
  * Forum posts
* Show a simple `<article>` code example

III. `<section>` Element

* Definition of `<section>`
* Purpose: groups related content under a specific topic
* Examples:

  * About Us
  * Services
  * School information
* Show a simple `<section>` code example

IV. `<aside>` Element

* Definition of `<aside>`
* Purpose: contains additional or supporting information
* Examples:

  * Related posts
  * Tips
  * Additional information
* Show a simple `<aside>` code example

V. Comparison of the Three Elements

* `<article>` → standalone content
* `<section>` → related/grouped content
* `<aside>` → additional/supporting content

VI. Combined Example

* Show how `<article>`, `<section>`, and `<aside>` can be used together
* Briefly explain the role of each element in the example

VII. Conclusion

* Review the purpose of the three elements
* Explain why semantic HTML helps organize webpages
